# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Virtual environment
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# SQLite database
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# IDE / Editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Testing / Coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Build / Distribution
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# FastAPI / Uvicorn temporary files
*.pid
```

**Important:** This will prevent `ecommerce.db` from being pushed to GitHub, which is what you generally want. Your database is generated locally when you run the application.

Your GitHub repository can therefore contain:

```text
ecommerce_api/
│
├── main.py
├── database.py
├── models.py
├── schemas.py
├── exceptions.py
├── requirements.txt
├── README.md
└── .gitignore
```
